{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nReviewed: 9e1116bd778ca19e640b80fa133c29f9a8724b5c\n\nVerified: The checkout is the reviewed tip. I reviewed the scoped diff against WI-977, its item-15 spec of record and owner ruling, PROCESS sections 3/5/6, the cited registry rows and their existing counterparts, and rubric K1/K2/K3/B1. I hunted fail-open claims/admission/provider launches first, then incorrect assignment, premature close/peel and lost state. The changed runtime paths resisted those scenarios. The prescribed run had 742 passes and two failures, both reproduced with base scripts and base tests. Eight new refusal regressions fail against the pre-change scripts on their intended behavior. No reviewed code was edited and no commit was made.\n\nCommands:\n- \"'`git rev-parse HEAD` -> `9e1116bd778ca19e640b80fa133c29f9a8724b5c`.\n- `git diff 55fe67d825ca7083dd349c0a3980c04d0d2afe7b...9e1116bd778ca19e640b80fa133c29f9a8724b5c -- . '\"':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/stage'\"'`, with targeted path diffs, Get-Content, rg and TOML cell comparisons -> inspected production changes, changed tests, migration/text changes, and referenced requirements without treating implementer notes or verdicts as evidence.\n- With `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` and `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES=C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-31b-leg26`, `C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider -n 2 --basetemp C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-31b-leg26/r2A/wi-977 tests/test_dispatch.py tests/test_dispatch_admission.py tests/test_integrate.py tests/test_integrate_station.py tests/test_agent_loop_worker.py tests/test_agent_loop_policy.py tests/test_handback.py tests/test_verdict_record.py te